			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852991">
									

<p>Downvoted for the test proposal with children, because the reason for proposing the test in the first place was not explicitly and compellingly identified. It felt like an immersion-breaking LOLFoundation moment. Note that I see absolutely nothing wrong with the concept of an amoral Foundation that uses children as D-class fodder, but it should be clear what additional information or benefit the Foundation hopes to gain from the experiment or procedure. Otherwise it feels like a lame joke.</p>
<p>Also, this doesn't make sense:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Since this date, no new active phases have been observed, despite the presence of individuals overnight.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The site's being monitored, contained, and systematically tested by the Foundation, but there's no experiment log for these individuals who were present overnight? What, did these individuals slip past Foundation security and spend the night while the researchers took a holiday? I'm sorry to say, it honestly feels like the author got sick of writing and gave up.</p>

