														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852985">
									

<p>HAHAHA no that was a happy coincidence.</p>
<p>There's not really any definitive information about the Scarlet King as far as I'm aware. Djorc's <a href="/dust-and-blood">Dust and Blood</a> is the closest thing we've got to an official mythology (you may have noticed that it's crosslinked by 231 and KTE-2013-Kappala-Mendes), but it still has some contradictions to other bits, especially if you consider 2317 to be Big Red. I think Kappala-Mendes is the only document with any information about the actual cult.</p>
<p>So, basically, if you want to write something about the Scarlet King, just do it! Really all you gotta have is the number 7, maybe some faux-Satanism sex cult business, and some ancient Middle Eastern magic. Or you could have none of that, since there is no canon after all, and Tufto's proposal implies that the idea of &quot;Scarlet King&quot; could really be a whole assortment of different beings and organizations. Pick out what you like from what's been written, ignore what you don't, and fill in the gaps yourself.</p>

							</div>

								
					
