<p>Delightful. (Never thought I'd say that about an insect scip.) This reminds me of various Series I scips, ones that don't offer much explicit insight into how the information in the article was obtained or deduced. The document just presents a weird thing in the universe that is somehow thoroughly understood by the Foundation; the scip's strength is the elegant simplicity and quirky cleverness of its weird idea.</p>
<p>I think that's a great approach even when aiming to fulfill modern standards. Arguably, a realistic containment procedures writeup is unlikely to contain the addenda and experiment logs that a lot of modern SCPs rely on to tell their story (because a realistic containment procedures writeup wouldn't be trying to tell a story).</p>

