			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852966">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Mystery/Horror</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> ACS header, basic layout, tons of audio recordings and exploration logs</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Series of sounds that resemble heartbeats, only found in deep lakes in Iceland, each with varying frequencies and loudness. The sounds are quite rare and cause mishaps in reality in a wide area around it.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The heartbeats last for 20-75 seconds, and range in frequency, loudness, and location. Heartbeats are relatively rare (1-3 times a year) but can be very troubling for the area around it.</p>
<p>Heartbeats come in pairs of 2 &quot;pumps&quot;, in this case, sound. Once a heartbeat starts, the pumps cause vibrations in the land, seemingly wavy land. Everything the sound can be heard is effected.<br />
Here's a list of each possible reality-bending scenario</p>
<ul>
<li>Vibrations in the land (wavy-like land)</li>
<li>Mountains deforming in a very unnatural way</li>
<li>Water vortexes</li>
<li>&quot;cracks&quot; in the air, where a black spot fills the crack</li>
<li>Clouds taking shape of humanoid figures</li>
<li>Talbon's Ring (a high-frequency ring that burst eardrums and rarely kills an organism)</li>
<li>The sky turning into dark, even during bright days</li>
<li>Temperature suddenly shooting up or increasing drastically</li>
<li>Altered heartbeats of humans (matches the lake's heartbeat)</li>
</ul>
<p>These are the only known effects of the heartbeat, but in later logs, more will appear (creepier and deadlier). A heartbeat can have serious effects on the ecosystem, and cause mass death amongst organisms, and heavily deformed land.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> A decent reality-bender that has some good potential, even though it probably has a LOT to work on.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Suggestions for editing needed :)</p>

